. The annex's rung-2 note says a bill that detains people *charged with* crimes shows the enforcement side only (`direction-only`). The bill says nothing about removing everyone else.\n- **Her press release, 2025-02-17:** her own words, in-term: \"dangerous illegal aliens are finally being detained and deported\". This also shows only the enforcement side. It never says \"only serious violent crimes\" (rung 2) or \"deport all\" (rungs 4–5).\n- **Dalilah Law press release:** it is about commercial driver's licenses, so it is `adjacent`.\n- **Campaign issues page:** it is written in the third person and undated, so it is `not-evidence`.\n\n`rests_on` and `needs_source` are both empty. I coded one quote (\"Thanks to the Laken Riley Act…\") as tier `none` and not quotable (`not-forward`), because it describes past action rather than what she would do.\n\nSeveral connected services need authorizing before their tools can be used: Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Harvey and WorkOS, through your claude.ai connector settings. The GitHub plugin also failed to connect, with a bad authorization header. None of these was needed for this task.","ttft_ms":13520,"type":"result","duration_ms":37298,"uuid":"f0bdd9ba-7260-44af-b958-46adb4b1b4c0","ttft_stream_ms":1784,"time_to_request_ms":190,"first_content_frame_ms":1784,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
